{
	"Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Admin Console Access from a New IP",
	"Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Initial Access / T1078.004\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Admin Console Access from a New IP\" or \"<ip>|Okta Admin Console Access from a New IP\"\n\nOkta Admin Console access (user.session.access_admin_app) from an IP address the administrator has not used for the Admin Console in the 14 days before the search window. Admin sessions from unfamiliar networks are a high-value signal for account takeover.\n\nFalse positives: admins travelling or on a new ISP. The first 14 days after install have less history, so expect more alerts then.",
